# No visible resize-handle symbol

Hard rule for diana’s dashboard (`/Users/diana/my-dashboard`) vision polaroids and other resizable cards.

## Ability stays; glyph never shows

- Keep the resize **hit target** (`.vision-pol-resize`, `.card-resize`, `.zone-resize`, `.oneoff-resize`, `.canvas-item-resize`) so drag-to-resize still works.
- Never show an L-corner, ⇲, grip lines, or any other **visible** resize symbol on polaroids / cards.

## Always

1. Keep `#no-resize-glyph` (and the overview-era `.vision-pol-resize` rules) killing `::before` / `::after` and any border/box-shadow/color that draws a corner mark.
2. When touching polaroid chrome or resize CSS, verify glyphs stay invisible in details + zoomed section views.
3. Prefer invisible hit targets (`background: none`, `border: 0`, `color: transparent`, `font-size: 0`) over decorative handles.

## Never

- Reintroduce a visible L in the polaroid white border
- Rely on “only hide on hover” — the glyph must be off in the resting state too
- Strip the resize node entirely just to hide the symbol (ability must remain)

## If a glyph is visible in a screenshot

Fix the CSS immediately (sync `everything.html` `#no-resize-glyph` with the permanent ban that includes `.vision-pol-resize`). Do not wait to be reminded.
